  "summary": "EPIC's overview page on License Plate Recognition systems explains how LPR works, surveys uses by US law enforcement, and raises informational-privacy concerns. It discusses state privacy laws, court cases on location tracking, and notes Maine and New Hampshire as the only states restricting LPR use.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "an LPR system in Nassau County, New York, can scan 8,000-10,000 license plates during an officer's eight-hour shift.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "Use of LPR systems should be subject to state privacy act requirements of notice, access and correction.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "Other than Maine, New Hampshire is the only other state to restrict the use of LPR systems.",
      "paragraph_idx": 12
    }
